# OzzBooks — Addendum: CBR → CBZ conversion (NAS file-maintenance task)

**This is a hand-off document, not app code.** It was drafted in a
Claude Code session working on the OzzBooks git repo (the "Comic/
graphic novel support" planning session, 2026-09-02), for execution by
a *different* session — one with real filesystem access to the NAS/Mac
mini, the same kind of session already doing the audiobook merging/
renaming work. That session should be able to follow this document on
its own, without having read the planning conversation it came from.

**Status: planned, not started.**

## Why this exists

`Ozzbooks_Addendum_Comics` (the OzzBooks app-side plan for native
comics/graphic novel support) settled on **`.cbz` as the only archive
format OzzBooks itself ingests** — no in-app RAR handling, no `unrar`
shell-out, no conversion-at-scan-time. That decision was made
specifically so this conversion work could be a normal NAS
file-maintenance task, done directly against the files, the same
category of work as the audiobook merging/renaming already happening —
rather than something the OzzBooks Node/TypeScript codebase needs to
solve internally.

**The goal**: every `.cbr` file under `/Volumes/Books/Comics` (67
series folders, ~3,440 files, a meaningful fraction of which are
currently `.cbr` per the original scoping notes) gets a faithful
`.cbz` sibling. Also worth checking: the handful of stray `.cbr` issues
(Dresden Files) that were found misfiled into the audiobook folders,
which is what originally surfaced the whole comics idea.

**No sequencing dependency with the OzzBooks app work.** OzzBooks scans
and ingests whatever's already `.cbz` immediately, and picks up newly
converted files automatically on its next nightly rescan — this
conversion pass can run in the background, in batches, over however
long it takes, without blocking or being blocked by the app-side build.

## Per-file conversion procedure

1. **Detect by magic bytes, not just the extension** — `Rar!\x1a\x07`
   for RAR, `PK\x03\x04` for zip. A `.cbr`-extensioned file that's
   already zip data internally (or vice versa) shows up occasionally in
   scanned/scene-released collections; this rescues it from needing
   conversion at all rather than either mishandling it or flagging it
   as broken.
2. **Skip if already done.** If a sibling file with the same base name
   and a `.cbz` extension already exists next to the `.cbr`, skip —
   idempotent by construction, safe to re-run this whole process across
   multiple work sessions without re-doing finished files. If such a
   sibling exists but looks unrelated (very different size/page count),
   flag for manual review rather than guessing which one is right.
3. **Extract** via `unrar x` (RARLab's official CLI — free for
   extraction use, current versions handle RAR5) into a scratch/temp
   directory. Treat **any non-zero exit code as a failure**, including
   RAR's own "non-fatal warning" codes, not just hard errors — don't
   produce a `.cbz` from a partial/suspect extraction. Clean up the
   scratch directory afterward regardless of success or failure (a
   try/finally, not just a happy-path `rm`) — matters at this file
   count, since leftover temp directories would otherwise accumulate
   across thousands of runs.
4. **Sanity-check the extraction**: if it produced zero recognized
   image files (`.jpg`/`.jpeg`/`.png`/`.gif`/`.webp`), this isn't a
   valid comic archive — don't produce a `.cbz`, flag for manual review
   (mislabeled file, or genuinely corrupt).
5. **Re-zip as a faithful, dumb repackage** — every extracted file
   included (including `ComicInfo.xml`), original filenames preserved,
   no renaming. **Entry order inside the zip doesn't matter** — OzzBooks'
   own page-serving logic always natural-sorts filenames at read time
   rather than trusting archive order (an explicit invariant on the app
   side, specifically so this conversion pass doesn't need to fuss over
   getting insertion order right). Whatever's convenient on this
   session's own toolchain — the `zip` CLI, a scripting language's zip
   library, whatever's idiomatic there — is fine; nothing here needs to
   match OzzBooks' own Node/`jszip` stack, since this document has no
   code dependency on that codebase at all.
6. **Output path**: same folder, same base filename as the original
   `.cbr`, just a `.cbz` extension. This matters beyond tidiness —
   OzzBooks derives a comic's series name from its *folder* path
   (first path segment under the Comics source root), so keeping the
   converted file in the exact same location is what makes it ingest
   correctly, not an incidental choice.
7. **Verify before calling it done**: list the new `.cbz`'s contents
   and confirm the recognized-image-file count matches what step 4
   found in the extraction — a lightweight check that nothing silently
   truncated during the re-zip, not a full pixel-level comparison.
8. **Move the original `.cbr` aside, never delete it.** Move it into a
   sibling folder named `zzzSource files` (or `Source`/`source files` —
   any of these already match `scan.ts`'s `BACKUP_FOLDER_RE` on the
   OzzBooks side). Two things this gets for free: the original stays
   recoverable as a safety net, and OzzBooks' own scanner already
   excludes anything under a folder matching that name — so the backed-
   up original won't show up as a confusing duplicate, and won't keep
   generating a "still needs conversion" `scan_issues` entry once it's
   out of the scanned tree. Actually deleting the backed-up originals
   later, to reclaim disk space, is a deliberate manual decision for
   another day — not something this pass does on its own.

## Explicitly out of scope for this pass

- **Renaming or reorganizing files/folders.** Keep format conversion
  and any file-hygiene/renaming pass separate, even if the audiobook
  workflow bundles both — a bad rename is much harder to untangle from
  inside a large batch conversion than on its own. If reorganization is
  wanted for the Comics library too, treat it as its own follow-up
  pass, after conversion is verified stable.
- **PDF or loose-image-folder comics.** Nothing to convert — these
  aren't RAR archives. (Both are separately flagged as fast-follow app
  work in `Ozzbooks_Addendum_Comics`, unaffected by this document.)
- **Editing `ComicInfo.xml` content.** Preserve it exactly as found;
  cleaning up metadata quality is a separate concern, not this pass's
  job.

## Progress visibility

Given the file count, expect this to run across multiple work sessions.
The idempotency check in step 2 makes re-running the whole pass safe at
any time, so no separate tracking file is strictly required — but a
short summary at the end of each run (converted / flagged for review /
already done / remaining) is worth keeping, if only so it's obvious at
a glance how much of the library is left. On the OzzBooks app side,
once ingestion is running, `scan_issues` for the Comics source doubles
as a live view of exactly which files are still waiting on this
conversion — worth checking there too, not just tracking separately.

